Directory ./rnp_experimental contains a second copy of rnp which has been
obtained from:
https://github.com/rnpgp/rnp

[commit 4f5c4e6e9b9a895762290bf03ed342ea8e69bbd2]

rnp_experimental is an unreleased RNP upstream snapshot. This fork builds
it on every channel, with ENABLE_CRYPTO_REFRESH, so it can decrypt
RFC 9580 PKESK v6 and SEIPDv2 messages.

A local patch for anonymous v6 PKESK packets is recorded in
../patches/rnp_experimental/ and listed in moz.yaml. It is already
applied to the sources in this directory. Each anonymous PKESK restarts
secret-key iteration, so a later recipient still decrypts.

For licensing information, please refer to the included documentation.

Updates to this copy are managed by "mach vendor". The configuration file is
at rnp_experimental/moz.yaml. Unlike ./rnp, this copy does not update
MIN_RNP_VERSION in RNPLib.sys.mjs.

    > cd comm/third_party/rnp_experimental

    # validate the YAML config file
    > mach vendor -v ./moz.yaml
    ./moz.yaml: OK

    # update to a specific upstream commit
    > mach vendor -r <commit> ./moz.yaml

    # If there are patches to apply in moz.yaml, the process is a little different
    > mach vendor ./moz.yaml --patch-mode none
    # followed by
    > mach vendor ./moz.yaml --patch-mode only

